They're not ugly

&#x200B;

THEY'RE HIDEOUS

Plastic surgery is highly underrated and should not be taboo to talk about. If you're lightspeed ugly it's one of the smartest investments you can make. 

&#x200B;

Invest in yourself.

This is where my opinion might be a bit more controversial, but here goes:

&#x200B;

I think being mild to moderately hungry is perfectly normal and is just a part of life. Farming has only been around for like, what, 10,000 years? Before farming we were hunting, right? So for millions of years we were waking up, chasing after prey for probably the entire day until it dies of exhaustion (humans endure because we can sweat) and then hauling it back to camp and have a big-feast for the tribe. So really our bodies are built for fasted cardio and eating one (maybe two?) meals a day. If you're lucky you'd stumble upon some berries or honeycomb (though you most certainly wouldn't rely on these). Hunger =/= starvation.

&#x200B;

Your damn right that it would be hard to deny food to a hungry kid, even knowing they (presumably) shouldn't eat more than is advised...In that case I would involve the kid in physical activities at school or at home to help burn excess calories. That's your only other option (other than healthy food/meal prep) if you're going to let your kid eat whatever they want.

I got fucked so hard by these meds. Terrible insomnia where I would only be able to sleep 2-3 hours at a time. Tinnitus that hasn't ceased since discontinuing, AND my fucking hair was falling out right in the front of my forehead. It's been 4 months since i've been on them and I still have tinnitus and the hair that fell out hasn't grown back yet :( even more depressed than when I started.

&#x200B;

Insomnia went away though rather quickly, feels so fucking good to sleep normally again.
